- [Joel] You mean they
have to build their cars,

728
00:28:25,438 --> 00:28:26,605
like a soapbox derby?

729
00:28:33,212 --> 00:28:35,013
- Look, I'll be along later.

730
00:28:35,915 --> 00:28:37,350
- How come?

731
00:28:37,350 --> 00:28:38,618
- I gotta make a call,
see if my mom's all right.

732
00:28:38,618 --> 00:28:39,552
- [Crow] At the mortuary.

733
00:28:39,552 --> 00:28:40,787
- Go ahead, we'll wait for you.

734
00:28:40,787 --> 00:28:43,022
- No, I'm gonna have
to go home for awhile.

735
00:28:45,892 --> 00:28:47,193
- Okay.

736
00:28:47,193 --> 00:28:48,293
See ya at Nick's, huh?

737
00:28:49,495 --> 00:28:50,730
- Phil.

738
00:28:50,730 --> 00:28:51,965
- [Tom] We're all gonna
die alone and afraid.

739
00:28:51,965 --> 00:28:53,398
- Yeah.
- Hold on to this for me.

740
00:28:54,700 --> 00:28:55,702
- [Joel] You know,
I'm kind of screwed up

741
00:28:55,702 --> 00:28:56,837
and anything can happen to me.

742
00:28:58,672 --> 00:29:00,407
- [Crow] I'd like a good smoke.

743
00:29:00,407 --> 00:29:01,340
- Where's Sonny?

744
00:29:01,340 --> 00:29:02,942
- [Crow] It's Cher.

745
00:29:02,942 --> 00:29:04,543
- Sonny comin' man?

746
00:29:04,543 --> 00:29:05,778
- Yeah, he'll be along later.

747
00:29:05,778 --> 00:29:06,678
- Let's cut out.

748
00:29:06,678 --> 00:29:07,513
- Yeah, crazy.

749
00:29:08,848 --> 00:29:11,885
- Now is that Brian
Dennehy or Charles Durning?

750
00:29:11,885 --> 00:29:13,118
- JJ This is a job
for Super Teen.

751
00:29:13,118 --> 00:29:15,322
I think I know where
I can find him.

752
00:29:17,857 --> 00:29:19,425
- [Crow] Teen-Mobile on.

753
00:29:19,425 --> 00:29:20,927
I've gotta get into
the Teen-Mobile.

754
00:29:20,927 --> 00:29:23,195
Zit guns set for high.

755
00:29:23,195 --> 00:29:24,497
- [Joel] Hey, it's Cannon.

756
00:29:26,933 --> 00:29:29,835
- [Tom] You can't walk out on
me, I'm Charles Foster Kane.

757
00:29:30,970 --> 00:29:33,640
(tires screech)

758
00:29:35,007 --> 00:29:38,010
- [Crow] Now we see Tom McHale
test a '53 Ford Victoria

759
00:29:38,010 --> 00:29:39,345
and it really performs.

760
00:29:39,345 --> 00:29:40,847
- [Tom] It's a big, bulky car.

761
00:29:40,847 --> 00:29:43,082
You see, it doesn't matter
how slow I go, I'll cut ya.

762
00:29:43,082 --> 00:29:44,550
My son's the editor.

763
00:29:44,550 --> 00:29:47,720
- [Crow] Hey, it's a Sunday
night NBC mystery movie.

764
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:51,090
- What is going on?
- Who is that?

765
00:29:51,090 --> 00:29:52,225
- [Joel] Wait a minute.

766
00:29:53,627 --> 00:29:56,528
- [Crow] Whoa, the
cut-away caught fire.

767
00:29:58,765 --> 00:30:01,633
Now on the border of
Czechoslovakia and East Germany.

768
00:30:03,435 --> 00:30:06,038
- [Tom] Ha, cute little
clown car. (laughs)

769
00:30:06,038 --> 00:30:07,573
Cute.

770
00:30:07,573 --> 00:30:09,242
- I'll get the gate.

771
00:30:10,410 --> 00:30:11,543
- [Tom] Vandals.

772
00:30:12,945 --> 00:30:13,813
- [Crow] Let's go vandals.

773
00:30:13,813 --> 00:30:15,482
Whoa.

774
00:30:15,482 --> 00:30:16,248
- They're young.

775
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:19,385
- Do you know your
way through, Jana?

776
00:30:19,385 --> 00:30:20,953
- Blindfolded.
- [Crow] Well, so be it.

777
00:30:20,953 --> 00:30:22,988
- You can still cancel out.
- Ask him.

778
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:25,492
- Okay, just don't forget
this run isn't banked.

779
00:30:25,492 --> 00:30:27,160
- It takes more
skill than speed.

780
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:29,028
- When you get to the fork,
go either left or right.

781
00:30:29,028 --> 00:30:30,297
Both of them wind up-

782
00:30:30,297 --> 00:30:31,263
- I've been through
here 1,000 times.

783
00:30:31,263 --> 00:30:32,465
How 'bout the other gate?

784
00:30:32,465 --> 00:30:33,667
- We'll take the highway around,

785
00:30:33,667 --> 00:30:34,867
have it open before
you get there.

786
00:30:34,867 --> 00:30:36,903
- Anything goes, Daddy-O.

787
00:30:36,903 --> 00:30:37,770
- Ooh, that hurt.

788
00:30:40,138 --> 00:30:42,008
- [Crow] You sound like Marlena
Dietrich all of a sudden.

789
00:30:42,008 --> 00:30:43,508
- You ready, Jana?

790
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:45,043
Phil?

791
00:30:45,043 --> 00:30:48,113
- [Tom] John Frankenheimer
directs Race for the Pizza.

792
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:52,418
- [Joel] Paul Newman
and Tom cruise

793
00:30:52,418 --> 00:30:54,820
in The Color of Days of Thunder.

794
00:30:54,820 --> 00:30:57,257
The car, Christine or Herbie.

795
00:30:57,257 --> 00:30:59,058
- [Tom] I like mine
with thin crust.

796
00:31:00,025 --> 00:31:01,393
- [Joel] Just like Ben Hur.

797
00:31:03,162 --> 00:31:05,163
- [Crow] I like
mine Chicago style.

798
00:31:05,163 --> 00:31:06,432
- I ain't buyin' no pizza.

799
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:09,602
- [Joel] Ooh, wait a minute.

800
00:31:09,602 --> 00:31:12,438
How'd he get on that side of
her, Tyco change-up track?

801
00:31:12,438 --> 00:31:13,438
- [Tom] Huh?

802
00:31:15,442 --> 00:31:17,510
- Hey, hold it, you.

803
00:31:17,510 --> 00:31:18,578
Hey, come back here.

804
00:31:18,578 --> 00:31:20,078
- [Crow] Here, have some gum.

805
00:31:20,078 --> 00:31:21,847
- Where you goin', kid?
- [Tom] Kid, I'm an adult.

806
00:31:21,847 --> 00:31:23,515
Like I'm only 43 and everything.

807
00:31:26,685 --> 00:31:29,522
(adventure music)

808
00:31:30,957 --> 00:31:32,492
- [Crow] Gotham city, 14 miles.

809
00:31:35,895 --> 00:31:36,762
- [Joel] Cutaway.

810
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:38,865
- [Crow] Cutaway.

811
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:41,633
- [Tom] Cutaway.

812
00:31:41,633 --> 00:31:46,605
♪ Cutaway chase game cutaway ♪

813
00:31:51,543 --> 00:31:54,947
- [Joel] Ah, stuffed
pizza and crazy bread.

814
00:31:54,947 --> 00:31:55,915
- [Tom] Pizza, pizza.

815
00:31:58,885 --> 00:32:01,620
(brakes screech)

816
00:32:03,055 --> 00:32:04,890
- He should be here
any second now.

817
00:32:06,258 --> 00:32:08,093
- [Crow] Our pert little racer's
wearing a wool, gabardine,

818
00:32:08,093 --> 00:32:10,028
slack and kicky modified trench.

819
00:32:10,028 --> 00:32:11,830
She's a real Deuce Coupe.

820
00:32:11,830 --> 00:32:12,665
- Hi.

821
00:32:12,665 --> 00:32:13,967
- [Joel] Danny Thomas.

822
00:32:13,967 --> 00:32:15,233
- I just don't believe it.

823
00:32:15,233 --> 00:32:17,237
- [Tom] The things I can
do with my Spirograph.

824
00:32:17,237 --> 00:32:18,805
- Where'd you pass him?

825
00:32:18,805 --> 00:32:20,272
- Just after the start.

826
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:22,042
- No one's ever beaten
him through there before.

827
00:32:22,042 --> 00:32:23,342
- [Crow] Well, no
one else has these.

828
00:32:23,342 --> 00:32:25,478
- He had engine trouble.

829
00:32:25,478 --> 00:32:26,878
- He had trouble all right.

830
00:32:26,878 --> 00:32:27,980
- [Tom] Me.

831
00:32:30,583 --> 00:32:31,383
There!

832
00:32:32,985 --> 00:32:35,253
- [Crow] Piece of British crap.

833
00:32:35,253 --> 00:32:38,157
(mumbles)

834
00:32:38,157 --> 00:32:40,158
And a chili pepper to burn my
gut, and order cheese bread.

835
00:32:40,158 --> 00:32:41,060
She's gonna do it.

836
00:32:42,462 --> 00:32:45,532
- [Tom] Pizza's here. (laughs)

837
00:32:46,698 --> 00:32:48,000
- I'm telling ya, baby.

838
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:49,902
If you were a man, I'd
knock your head off.

839
00:32:49,902 --> 00:32:51,270
- You said that once before.

840
00:32:52,272 --> 00:32:53,472
- Ran me off.

841
00:32:53,472 --> 00:32:54,440
- What do you mean?
- The road?

842
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,942
- [Tom] No, just ran me off.

843
00:32:55,942 --> 00:32:57,777
- This maniac here forced
me onto a dirt road.

844
00:32:57,777 --> 00:32:59,778
- Like I said, anything goes.

845
00:32:59,778 --> 00:33:02,315
- Cole Porter.
- You didn't wreck your car?

846
00:33:02,315 --> 00:33:04,050
- No, but I almost
hit a night watchman.

847
00:33:04,050 --> 00:33:06,252
- [Man] You mean the old
guy with the station wagon?

848
00:33:06,252 --> 00:33:07,553
- That's right.

849
00:33:07,553 --> 00:33:09,055
He was comin' up that dirt road.

850
00:33:09,055 --> 00:33:11,557
I bet he jumped right out
of his winter underwear.

851
00:33:12,558 --> 00:33:14,127
- Very funny.

852
00:33:14,127 --> 00:33:16,428
If he got my license
number, I've had it.

853
00:33:16,428 --> 00:33:17,263
- Aw, relax pal.

854
00:33:17,263 --> 00:33:18,430
He's probably so scared,

855
00:33:18,430 --> 00:33:19,898
he doesn't even
remember his own name.

856
00:33:19,898 --> 00:33:22,135
- [Crow] Carl, my name's Carl.

857
00:33:22,135 --> 00:33:24,037
- But I got his license number.

858
00:33:25,672 --> 00:33:28,207
(upbeat music)

859
00:33:33,145 --> 00:33:35,548
- [Crow] A pancake,
no, we ordered pizza.

860
00:33:35,548 --> 00:33:36,815
- Later, baby?

861
00:33:36,815 --> 00:33:37,950
- Okay.

862
00:33:37,950 --> 00:33:39,285
- [Tom] I'll get the syrup.

863
00:33:42,355 --> 00:33:43,388
- I don't know about the
rest of you gourmets,

864
00:33:43,388 --> 00:33:44,723
but I could go for another one.

865
00:33:44,723 --> 00:33:46,192
- I'm buying.

866
00:33:46,192 --> 00:33:48,593
Come on, don't be a bad sport.

867
00:33:48,593 --> 00:33:51,430
- Can't you leave him
alone, he's upset.

868
00:33:51,430 --> 00:33:53,465
- It's tough enough
losing the race.

869
00:33:53,465 --> 00:33:55,367
I don't want him to
go home hungry too.

870
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:56,835
- [Joel] Yeah, and besides that.

871
00:33:58,303 --> 00:34:00,540
- [Crow] Cops, it's filmed
on location 20 years ago.

872
00:34:01,940 --> 00:34:03,910
- [Tom] Hey, you're facing
the wrong way for the driving.

873
00:34:03,910 --> 00:34:05,678
- Give me your attention please.

874
00:34:05,678 --> 00:34:07,347
- [Crow] My name's Phil
and I'm an alcoholic.

875
00:34:07,347 --> 00:34:08,815
- Hi, Phil.
- Hi, Phil.

876
00:34:08,815 --> 00:34:10,883
- Who owns the blue sports
job out there, HGN227?

877
00:34:12,218 --> 00:34:13,887
- Right here.
- Step out here, will ya.

878
00:34:15,187 --> 00:34:18,123
- [Tom] Oh, this Walkman
works really well.

879
00:34:20,158 --> 00:34:21,827
- [Joel] Well, we usually
beat you up right here,

880
00:34:21,827 --> 00:34:24,230
but there's a camera on so
you'll have to get in back.

881
00:34:24,230 --> 00:34:25,163
- [Tom] I'll ride in
the back with him, Andy.

882
00:34:25,163 --> 00:34:26,598
I want, want a donut?

883
00:34:26,598 --> 00:34:28,233
Just kidding, a
little cop humor.

884
00:34:29,568 --> 00:34:31,870
- What?
- Oh, no, no, no.

885
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:38,043
- [Crow] 7:15, Gannon and
I headed back downtown.

886
00:34:39,512 --> 00:34:40,813
De bunco.

887
00:34:40,813 --> 00:34:41,847
- Okay, what's the charge?

888
00:34:41,847 --> 00:34:43,115
- [Tom] Al Bundy?

889
00:34:44,517 --> 00:34:49,488
- Destruction of property,
trespassing, reckless driving,

890
00:34:50,355 --> 00:34:52,158
hit and run, and manslaughter.

891
00:34:52,158 --> 00:34:53,492
- Hit and run and manslaughter?

892
00:34:53,492 --> 00:34:54,927
- [Crow] Oh, that was
just me getting nuts,

893
00:34:54,927 --> 00:34:56,195
I'll change that.

894
00:34:56,195 --> 00:34:57,130
- Wait a minute, what
are you talkin' about,

895
00:34:57,130 --> 00:34:58,798
hit and run and manslaughter?

896
00:34:58,798 --> 00:35:00,733
- The accident you
had in the park.

897
00:35:00,733 --> 00:35:01,533
Remember?

898
00:35:01,533 --> 00:35:02,568
- What accident?

899
00:35:02,568 --> 00:35:03,668
Where?

900
00:35:03,668 --> 00:35:05,705
- The car you sideswiped
on Canyon Road.

901
00:35:06,938 --> 00:35:08,740
A kid died in that wreck?

902
00:35:08,740 --> 00:35:10,577
- Sideswiped?

903
00:35:10,577 --> 00:35:11,477
What car?

904
00:35:11,477 --> 00:35:12,278
What are you talking about?

905
00:35:12,278 --> 00:35:13,778
- '49 For blue coupe.

906
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:16,115
Kid's name was-

907
00:35:16,115 --> 00:35:17,082
- [Crow] James Dean?

908
00:35:17,082 --> 00:35:19,118
- Leonard DeMarco.

909
00:35:19,118 --> 00:35:22,155
- [Tom] Hey, I got a
felt pen by that name.

910
00:35:22,155 --> 00:35:23,088
- [Crow] DeMarco?

911
00:35:23,088 --> 00:35:24,657
- Sonny?

912
00:35:24,657 --> 00:35:25,925
- [Joel] Dad!
- Dead?

913
00:35:30,328 --> 00:35:32,432
- [Cop] Police examination
having found your vehicle free

914
00:35:32,432 --> 00:35:35,000
from scratches, dents,
or damage of any kind,

915
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:38,170
upholds your plea of not guilty
to charges four and five:

916
00:35:38,170 --> 00:35:39,872
hit and run and manslaughter.

917
00:35:39,872 --> 00:35:41,073
- [Crow] Is he talkin'
to the narrator?

918
00:35:41,073 --> 00:35:42,542
- As for charge
one, two, and three:

919
00:35:42,542 --> 00:35:44,243
destruction of city
property, trespassing,

920
00:35:44,243 --> 00:35:46,112
and reckless driving.
- Look, I know all that.

921
00:35:46,112 --> 00:35:47,547
The judge read it to me, okay?

922
00:35:47,547 --> 00:35:48,780
- [Tom] Do I get the job or not?

923
00:35:48,780 --> 00:35:50,282
- Just wanted to make
sure you understood.

924
00:35:50,282 --> 00:35:52,685
- [Radio] Cancel your prowler
call, 12 and 15 have handled.

925
00:35:52,685 --> 00:35:54,687
- [Joel] So you enjoy Adam 12?

926
00:35:54,687 --> 00:35:55,888
- [Radio] 379 M.

927
00:35:58,123 --> 00:35:59,358
- Put a guy on probation,

928
00:35:59,358 --> 00:36:02,828
take away his driver's
license, understood.

929
00:36:02,828 --> 00:36:05,097
- He could've made it a
lot worse on you, Phil.

930
00:36:05,097 --> 00:36:06,532
I'd say you were pretty lucky.

931
00:36:06,532 --> 00:36:07,433
- Lucky?
- Look at his shirt.

932
00:36:07,433 --> 00:36:08,600
You call this lucky?

933
00:36:11,537 --> 00:36:14,840
- Look, Mr. Wooster, my best
friend was buried this morning.

934
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:16,608
Yesterday I lost my job.

935
00:36:16,608 --> 00:36:18,912
I can't drive a car for
a whole stinkin' year.

936
00:36:18,912 --> 00:36:20,478
- [Crow] Uh huh, and?

937
00:36:20,478 --> 00:36:22,180
- I'm sorry about
the DeMarco kid.

938
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:23,382
Close, huh?

939
00:36:23,382 --> 00:36:25,483
- Some guys have got brothers.

940
00:36:25,483 --> 00:36:26,452
I had Sonny.

941
00:36:26,452 --> 00:36:27,853
- Where are your folks, Phil?

942
00:36:27,853 --> 00:36:29,588
- I ran away when I was 14.

943
00:36:29,588 --> 00:36:32,492
The old man and old lady didn't
even bother to look for me.

944
00:36:32,492 --> 00:36:34,427
- Well, I'll let
you in on something.

945
00:36:34,427 --> 00:36:35,728
I ran away when I was 15.

946
00:36:35,728 --> 00:36:36,962
- [Crow] Does that
tell you anything?

947
00:36:36,962 --> 00:36:38,197
- So what?

948
00:36:38,197 --> 00:36:39,498
- I understand you
work for a carnival?

949
00:36:39,498 --> 00:36:40,700
- Yeah.

950
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:41,667
- [Tom] Yeah, I bit
the heads off chickens.

951
00:36:41,667 --> 00:36:43,268
- Daredevil driving act.

952
00:36:43,268 --> 00:36:45,972
I didn't have much
sense in those days.

953
00:36:45,972 --> 00:36:47,540
- Is that why you
drive like an idiot?

954
00:36:47,540 --> 00:36:49,075
- What are you talking about?

955
00:36:49,075 --> 00:36:51,210
I know what I can do and I
know what that car can do.

956
00:36:51,210 --> 00:36:52,210
I've never been in an accident.

957
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:53,378
I've never caused one.

958
00:36:53,378 --> 00:36:54,913
- Yeah, I know Phil.

959
00:36:54,913 --> 00:36:57,583
You're a real fine driver,
but what about a job?

960
00:36:57,583 --> 00:36:58,417
- [Crow] Does that tickle?

961
00:36:59,352 --> 00:37:01,287
- I don't know.

962
00:37:01,287 --> 00:37:02,822
I don't have a driver's license.

963
00:37:02,822 --> 00:37:04,190
The law fixed that.

964
00:37:04,190 --> 00:37:05,825
- Well see what you can find.

965
00:37:05,825 --> 00:37:08,093
You can't get anything by next
week, I'll give you a hand.

966
00:37:08,093 --> 00:37:09,362
- [Crow] Not a job, just a hand.

967
00:37:09,362 --> 00:37:10,562
I have your friend's
hand in the drawer.

968
00:37:10,562 --> 00:37:11,963
- Can I go now?

969
00:37:11,963 --> 00:37:13,465
- Unless you want some coffee.

970
00:37:16,068 --> 00:37:17,870
- [Tom] I'll get the cream.

971
00:37:17,870 --> 00:37:18,703
- Phil?

972
00:37:20,072 --> 00:37:20,940
- Yeah.

973
00:37:20,940 --> 00:37:21,940
- Anytime you need me.

974
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:22,908
- [Crow] I'll be this big.

975
00:37:22,908 --> 00:37:23,708
- I'm here.

976
00:37:27,313 --> 00:37:28,713
- [Tom] You know, Phil,
I know a wiener man.

977
00:37:28,713 --> 00:37:30,082
He owns a hot dog stand.

978
00:37:30,082 --> 00:37:31,983
You know, he gives me
everything from wieners on down.

979
00:37:31,983 --> 00:37:33,018
- What are you
gonna do now, man?

980
00:37:33,018 --> 00:37:34,487
- [Crow] Oh, smoke.

981
00:37:34,487 --> 00:37:35,822
- I dunno, I haven't even
given it much thought.

982
00:37:37,290 --> 00:37:40,325
- Why don't you try Barney? He
might give you a job singin'.

983
00:37:40,325 --> 00:37:41,160
- Yeah.

984
00:37:42,428 --> 00:37:43,662
Hey, Duke.

985
00:37:43,662 --> 00:37:45,197
Where does that
crazy chick live?

986
00:37:45,197 --> 00:37:46,732
- Francis Farmer?
- Who, Jana?

987
00:37:46,732 --> 00:37:48,233
- Yeah, Jana.

988
00:37:48,233 --> 00:37:49,402
- I didn't think you'd be
so anxious to see her again.

989
00:37:49,402 --> 00:37:50,870
- [Crow] Well, I need
my ice pick back.

990
00:37:50,870 --> 00:37:52,170
- Remember when I told
you I took the right fork

991
00:37:52,170 --> 00:37:53,238
during the race?

992
00:37:53,238 --> 00:37:54,473
- Yeah.

993
00:37:54,473 --> 00:37:55,942
- [Joel] Well I actually
used a salad fork.

994
00:37:55,942 --> 00:37:57,643
It's kinda dumb.
- In the mountain there's

995
00:37:57,643 --> 00:37:59,245
a place on top, a
place where you can see

996
00:37:59,245 --> 00:38:00,478
almost all the way down.

997
00:38:00,478 --> 00:38:01,947
- Aw, man, every
lover knows that.

998
00:38:01,947 --> 00:38:03,082
- Yeah, but when I was
up there and looked down,

999
00:38:03,082 --> 00:38:04,783
I didn't see
anybody ahead of me.

1000
00:38:04,783 --> 00:38:07,653
That means that Jana took
the left fork, right?

1001
00:38:07,653 --> 00:38:09,188
- [Tom] Left, right.

1002
00:38:09,188 --> 00:38:10,455
- Third base.
- Third base.

1003
00:38:10,455 --> 00:38:14,060
- Sonny was killed
on the left fork.

1004
00:38:14,060 --> 00:38:15,460
- [Crow] Let's go there now.

1005
00:38:16,328 --> 00:38:18,363
(melancholy music)

1006
00:38:18,363 --> 00:38:19,432
- That's it.

1007
00:38:19,432 --> 00:38:20,800
Nice little chicken coup, huh?

1008
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:24,003
- Thanks, Duke.
(Crow squawks)

1009
00:38:24,003 --> 00:38:26,572
- [Joel] Isn't that where
Darren and Samantha live?

1010
00:38:28,673 --> 00:38:30,075
- Hey, Sherlock.

1011
00:38:30,075 --> 00:38:32,277
She's a better girl
than you think she is.

1012
00:38:32,277 --> 00:38:34,113
- Sure.
- Thank you, Watson.

1013
00:38:35,247 --> 00:38:36,848
- [Crow] Hey, wait,
that's his ride.

1014
00:38:37,950 --> 00:38:38,983
Means I have to walk.

1015
00:38:40,552 --> 00:38:43,888
(suspenseful music)

1016
00:38:43,888 --> 00:38:46,625
- [Joel] Yeah, sure, make
yourself at home, boy.

1017
00:38:46,625 --> 00:38:47,860
- [Tom] Nah, just gonna
do a little tinkering.

1018
00:38:47,860 --> 00:38:49,862
Gonna putz around
a little, you know.

1019
00:38:51,797 --> 00:38:54,167
- [Crow] I hate all of
you, you inanimate objects.

1020
00:38:54,167 --> 00:38:56,135
You mock me by your silence.

1021
00:38:56,135 --> 00:38:58,103
- [Joel] Come on, I can take ya.

1022
00:38:58,103 --> 00:39:00,672
- [Tom] It's a George
Barris custom car kit.

1023
00:39:05,812 --> 00:39:07,813
- [Crow] You're my best
friend in the world.

1024
00:39:07,813 --> 00:39:09,715
No one understands me.

1025
00:39:09,715 --> 00:39:11,017
(door bangs)

1026
00:39:11,017 --> 00:39:12,485
- [Tom] Oh, you've
lost, oh that's the mom.

1027
00:39:12,485 --> 00:39:14,453
- Trying to find out what
makes it run so fast?

1028
00:39:14,453 --> 00:39:15,955
- [Joel] Yeah, what does that?

1029
00:39:18,590 --> 00:39:20,993
- You ran Sonny DeMarco
off the road, didn't ya?

1030
00:39:22,093 --> 00:39:23,762
Ran him off just
like you did me.

1031
00:39:26,565 --> 00:39:27,433
- Want some?

1032
00:39:28,567 --> 00:39:29,768
(thuds)

1033
00:39:29,768 --> 00:39:31,037
- I hate Granny Smith's.
- I want an answer.

1034
00:39:31,037 --> 00:39:33,205
- He was still at the
gardens when we left.

1035
00:39:33,205 --> 00:39:34,840
- There's a shortcut
to Canyon Road.

1036
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,308
He must have gotten
there ahead of you.

1037
00:39:36,308 --> 00:39:39,378
- If your friend had too much
to drink, don't blame me.

1038
00:39:40,847 --> 00:39:43,248
- That's a new headlight,
and that's touch up paint.

1039
00:39:43,248 --> 00:39:44,483
Now admit it.

1040
00:39:44,483 --> 00:39:46,785
- Leave me alone or
I'll call the police.

1041
00:39:46,785 --> 00:39:48,820
- [Crow] No, my
head's not an apple.

1042
00:39:48,820 --> 00:39:50,790
- You admit you killed Sonny.

1043
00:39:50,790 --> 00:39:53,758
- I almost ran off myself,
smashed my headlight.

1044
00:39:53,758 --> 00:39:54,860
- You liar!

1045
00:39:54,860 --> 00:39:56,162
- If I forced him off,

1046
00:39:56,162 --> 00:39:58,063
my right fender
would've been smashed.

1047
00:39:58,930 --> 00:40:00,732
- You're right.

1048
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:02,133
- Now kiss me.
- I'm sorry.

1049
00:40:04,737 --> 00:40:06,405
- [Tom] I'll have
that apple now.

1050
00:40:12,110 --> 00:40:13,578
- All I want's coffee.

1051
00:40:13,578 --> 00:40:15,747
- Two coffees,
black, huh, honey.

1052
00:40:15,747 --> 00:40:16,548
- [Tom] Thanks, mom.

1053
00:40:16,548 --> 00:40:17,450
Nice caboose.

1054
00:40:17,450 --> 00:40:18,550
What am I saying?

1055
00:40:18,550 --> 00:40:19,885
- I gotta check somethin'.

1056
00:40:19,885 --> 00:40:20,820
- What?

1057
00:40:20,820 --> 00:40:22,187
- My check.
- This.

1058
00:40:24,857 --> 00:40:26,158
- What is it?

1059
00:40:26,158 --> 00:40:27,693
- I don't know.

1060
00:40:27,693 --> 00:40:29,628
Sonny gave it to me
just before the race.

1061
00:40:29,628 --> 00:40:31,463
- [Crow] I think it was
the key to his heart.

1062
00:40:31,463 --> 00:40:32,665
- Looks ordinary enough.

1063
00:40:33,898 --> 00:40:36,068
- [Tom] Ah, here's Peggy
Lee with the coffee.

1064
00:40:37,068 --> 00:40:38,037
- [Joel] She's a tramp.

1065
00:40:38,037 --> 00:40:39,103
- Yeah, that's the trouble.

1066
00:40:40,238 --> 00:40:41,707
- With Tribbles?

1067
00:40:41,707 --> 00:40:43,608
- Do you really think
somebody did it on purpose?

1068
00:40:43,608 --> 00:40:44,710
- You saw the skid marks.

1069
00:40:44,710 --> 00:40:45,878
- [Crow] On my underwear.

1070
00:40:45,878 --> 00:40:47,780
- That's it, come on.

1071
00:40:47,780 --> 00:40:50,715
- He didn't say one word the
whole time I was at the table.

1072
00:40:50,715 --> 00:40:52,050
- Sonny wasn't meek, baby.

1073
00:40:53,118 --> 00:40:55,253
He was scared.
- Real scared.

1074
00:40:55,253 --> 00:40:56,088
- Plenty scared.

1075
00:40:57,288 --> 00:40:58,790
- What kind of scared?
- I went to his house

1076
00:40:58,790 --> 00:41:01,593
that day and I found that, oh,
oh, this isn't a flashback.

1077
00:41:01,593 --> 00:41:02,393
Sorry.

1078
00:41:03,762 --> 00:41:05,030
- [Tom] What is it?

1079
00:41:05,030 --> 00:41:06,498
- Where were you? Did
you leave the iron on?

1080
00:41:06,498 --> 00:41:07,700
- Did you see Sonny's mother?

1081
00:41:07,700 --> 00:41:08,867
- Yeah, the nurse only
let me see her for

1082
00:41:08,867 --> 00:41:10,135
about five minutes.

1083
00:41:10,135 --> 00:41:11,770
- What about the key?

1084
00:41:11,770 --> 00:41:14,005
- Says it belongs
to his gym locker.

1085
00:41:15,407 --> 00:41:16,875
Jana, I think we're
onto something.

1086
00:41:16,875 --> 00:41:18,710
- [Tom] Well would you
let the audience in on it?

1087
00:41:18,710 --> 00:41:20,712
- She asked me if I knew about
a bank account Sonny opened

1088
00:41:20,712 --> 00:41:21,547
in her name.

1089
00:41:22,447 --> 00:41:25,317
A bank account for 5,000 skins.

1090
00:41:25,317 --> 00:41:27,485
- [Crow] Oh, he was a trapper.

1091
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:28,320
- [Joel] Check it out.

1092
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:30,022
Bruce's gym and church.

1093
00:41:33,192 --> 00:41:35,460
- [Tom] Oh, I see, it's
a secretarial school.

1094
00:41:36,328 --> 00:41:37,428
- Can I help you, bud?

1095
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:41,167
- Yeah, I gotta get
somethin' out of a locker.

1096
00:41:41,167 --> 00:41:42,968
- Nobody but members
is allowed back there.

1097
00:41:42,968 --> 00:41:44,537
- [Joel] Hey, it's Joe Cocker.

1098
00:41:44,537 --> 00:41:46,405
- Well look, a buddy of mine
died and his mother asked me

1099
00:41:46,405 --> 00:41:47,973
to clean out his locker.

1100
00:41:47,973 --> 00:41:49,040
- Yeah?

1101
00:41:49,040 --> 00:41:50,275
What's his name?

1102
00:41:50,275 --> 00:41:51,243
- [Crow] Or why can't
he do it himself?

1103
00:41:51,243 --> 00:41:53,312
- DeMarco, Leonard DeMarco.

1104
00:41:53,312 --> 00:41:56,248
- [Tom] I can see
through your clothes now.

1105
00:41:56,248 --> 00:41:57,950
- I never heard
nothin' about it.

1106
00:41:57,950 --> 00:41:59,252
- Well, anyway, he
had an auto accident.

1107
00:41:59,252 --> 00:42:00,185
Now can I get his stuff?

1108
00:42:00,185 --> 00:42:01,353
- I'll take care of it.

1109
00:42:02,453 --> 00:42:04,557
- I got his key right here.

1110
00:42:04,557 --> 00:42:07,058
- Couldn't help you
if I wanted to, fella.

1111
00:42:07,058 --> 00:42:08,260
Gym policy.

1112
00:42:08,260 --> 00:42:10,395
- Oh, come on, mac,
only take five minutes.

1113
00:42:10,395 --> 00:42:12,063
- Look, fella, I'm busy.

1114
00:42:12,063 --> 00:42:13,865
Now hand over the key,
I'll take care of it later.

1115
00:42:13,865 --> 00:42:16,002
- I'll just keep it
until you do, Jack.

1116
00:42:16,968 --> 00:42:18,437
- [Joel] Jack, fella?

1117
00:42:18,437 --> 00:42:20,072
- [Crow] Say those pants
are kinda high, aren't they?

1118
00:42:20,072 --> 00:42:21,273
- Let's have it, fella.

1119
00:42:24,810 --> 00:42:25,643
- Sure.

1120
00:42:28,413 --> 00:42:29,782
- [Crow] Thanks, come again.

1121
00:42:34,052 --> 00:42:36,588
(upbeat music)

1122
00:42:40,625 --> 00:42:41,827
- Come on, Joel, hurry up.

1123
00:42:41,827 --> 00:42:44,663
- Okay, do you know
your way through, Jana?

1124
00:42:44,663 --> 00:42:45,932
- Blindfolded.

1125
00:42:45,932 --> 00:42:47,733
- You can cancel.

1126
00:42:47,733 --> 00:42:48,967
- Ask him.

1127
00:42:48,967 --> 00:42:51,170
- All right, Cambot,
roll that race footage.

1128
00:42:51,170 --> 00:42:53,905
On your marks, get set, go!

1129
00:42:55,975 --> 00:42:58,810
(car motors roar)

1130
00:43:02,413 --> 00:43:04,350
(yells)

1131
00:43:11,490 --> 00:43:13,725
Darn fool kids.

1132
00:43:13,725 --> 00:43:15,727
(yells)

1133
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:20,898
- Comin' up to the car.

1134
00:43:22,935 --> 00:43:27,272
- Okay, and now you both
win a delicious pizza.

1135
00:43:27,272 --> 00:43:29,273
- Wait, where's Joel?

1136
00:43:29,273 --> 00:43:31,577
Oh no, we've killed him.

1137
00:43:31,577 --> 00:43:35,047
- Joel Robinson dead at 31.

1138
00:43:35,047 --> 00:43:37,148
- I was just kiddin', you guys.

1139
00:43:37,148 --> 00:43:42,153
(alarm buzzes)
(everyone yells)

1140
00:43:51,797 --> 00:43:53,565
- [Crow] Boy, good thing
we were thrown clear

1141
00:43:53,565 --> 00:43:54,833
of those cars, huh?

1142
00:43:56,002 --> 00:43:57,468
- Don't you think
we better wait.

1143
00:43:57,468 --> 00:43:58,637
There may be someone there.

1144
00:43:58,637 --> 00:44:00,638
- Look, we might
even be too late now.

1145
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:02,140
- How you gonna get
in without a key?

1146
00:44:02,140 --> 00:44:03,008
- With this?

1147
00:44:03,008 --> 00:44:04,510
That's what this is for.

1148
00:44:04,510 --> 00:44:05,343
Now give me the flashlight
and get back in the car.

1149
00:44:05,343 --> 00:44:07,045
- I'm going with you.

1150
00:44:07,045 --> 00:44:09,080
- I said get back in the car.

1151
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:11,617
- You leave me here and I won't
be here when you get back.

1152
00:44:11,617 --> 00:44:13,752
- [Tom] Hey, remember
what he did to the apple.

1153
00:44:13,752 --> 00:44:17,723
- All right, come on, bull head.

1154
00:44:17,723 --> 00:44:19,223
- [Crow] Dickweed.

1155
00:44:23,695 --> 00:44:24,930
- [Joel] I don't think
we're ever gonna find

1156
00:44:24,930 --> 00:44:26,365
any night crawlers.

1157
00:44:31,470 --> 00:44:33,005
- [Crow] Keep it on my ankle.

1158
00:44:36,942 --> 00:44:40,478
- [Joel] Would you please.
(metal clangs)

1159
00:44:40,478 --> 00:44:43,448
(suspenseful music)

1160
00:44:47,185 --> 00:44:52,157
♪ Dum dum dum dum
dum dum dum dum ♪

1161
00:44:54,893 --> 00:44:57,395
- [Tom] This place must have
a wood-burning Nautilus.

1162
00:44:57,395 --> 00:44:59,197
- [Crow] All that
lumber back there.

1163
00:45:00,565 --> 00:45:02,067
- [Joel] Got to think.

1164
00:45:02,067 --> 00:45:04,603
Must try to think,
but too stupid.

1165
00:45:07,705 --> 00:45:09,742
- [Tom] Well, back to
cat burglar school.

1166
00:45:17,648 --> 00:45:19,752
- [Crow] All right, Sonny's
mom asked me to clean out

1167
00:45:19,752 --> 00:45:23,322
his locker and that's
just what I intend to do.

1168
00:45:23,322 --> 00:45:24,155
Come on.

1169
00:45:28,527 --> 00:45:30,062
- [Joel] Yeah, I like to watch.

1170
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:37,202
- [Tom] It helps if you hop.

1171
00:45:43,208 --> 00:45:45,410
- This must be it.

1172
00:45:45,410 --> 00:45:46,945
- [Crow] Yep, just as I
thought, nitrogen-filled,

1173
00:45:46,945 --> 00:45:48,647
double-glazed, triple-pane
Andersen Windows.

1174
00:45:48,647 --> 00:45:49,748
This should be easy.

1175
00:45:50,882 --> 00:45:52,217
- [Joel] I think we can
squeeze through there.

1176
00:45:52,217 --> 00:45:53,052
You go first.

1177
00:45:55,787 --> 00:45:57,522
- Give me some light.

1178
00:46:04,162 --> 00:46:05,897
- [Tom] Ow, that's
my nose, ow, oh.

1179
00:46:08,433 --> 00:46:10,802
Hey, it's the Sunday
mystery movie out there.

1180
00:46:14,540 --> 00:46:15,773
- [Crow] That's it.

1181
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:17,508
In you Pixies come
through the window.

1182
00:46:20,578 --> 00:46:22,547
- [Joel] Bruce's Gym,
now with three full

1183
00:46:22,547 --> 00:46:23,715
pieces of equipment.

1184
00:46:27,820 --> 00:46:29,488
- [Tom] On my
ankle, like I said.

1185
00:46:32,757 --> 00:46:34,693
- [Crow] Hey, nice
rattle collection.

1186
00:46:36,595 --> 00:46:37,428
(Bell rings)
- Oh, don't ring

1187
00:46:37,428 --> 00:46:39,330
the bike bell.

1188
00:46:39,330 --> 00:46:40,732
- [Bruce] Bruce's Gym.

1189
00:46:40,732 --> 00:46:41,667
- [Tom] Hey it's the
reporter from Citizen Cane.

1190
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:43,335
- [Bruce] We're closed now.

1191
00:46:43,335 --> 00:46:44,235
Drop by tomorrow morning.

1192
00:46:44,235 --> 00:46:45,603
I said tomorrow morning.

1193
00:46:45,603 --> 00:46:47,005
- [Crow] Come in
through the window.

1194
00:46:47,005 --> 00:46:47,940
I'll leave it open.

1195
00:46:49,742 --> 00:46:52,477
- [Joel] Let's make
shadow puppets together.

1196
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:57,015
- [Tom] They came in through

1197
00:46:57,015 --> 00:46:58,250
the bathroom
window, didn't they?

1198
00:46:58,250 --> 00:46:59,785
- [Crow] Protected
by a silver spoon.

1199
00:46:59,785 --> 00:47:01,353
- [Tom] Quick under the barbell.

1200
00:47:02,553 --> 00:47:04,088
- [Crow] Quick, get
into the coin slot.

1201
00:47:04,088 --> 00:47:05,557
- It's too obvious.

1202
00:47:05,557 --> 00:47:08,360
The boy wasn't intelligent
enough to choose the obvious.

1203
00:47:08,360 --> 00:47:09,628
- Maybe.

1204
00:47:09,628 --> 00:47:10,928
- I don't know why you
couldn't have done it

1205
00:47:10,928 --> 00:47:12,330
by yourself.
- Give me that.

1206
00:47:12,330 --> 00:47:13,165
- The shower.

1207
00:47:14,198 --> 00:47:16,067
- [Joel] Oh,
Daddy-O, you're such-

1208
00:47:16,067 --> 00:47:17,735
- 209, instead of
waiting for me.

1209
00:47:17,735 --> 00:47:19,103
- I wanted you here
when I opened it.

1210
00:47:19,103 --> 00:47:20,405
- [Crow] You think you're funny.

1211
00:47:20,405 --> 00:47:21,807
- Who's going to take it?

1212
00:47:21,807 --> 00:47:24,408
It's not possible you
think I don't trust you.

1213
00:47:25,610 --> 00:47:27,545
- [Bruce] Just wanted
you here, that's all.

1214
00:47:27,545 --> 00:47:30,182
- I assure you, if I
didn't trust you 100%.

1215
00:47:30,182 --> 00:47:32,117
- I'd trust you 60%.
- I wouldn't even

1216
00:47:32,117 --> 00:47:33,918
have considered you
for this operation.

1217
00:47:33,918 --> 00:47:35,387
- [Tom] I need an operation.

1218
00:47:35,387 --> 00:47:37,288
- Hey, you know the rules
about smoking in here.

1219
00:47:37,288 --> 00:47:40,425
Smoke of the cigar, it's
like exotic perfume compared

1220
00:47:40,425 --> 00:47:42,027
with the air in here.

1221
00:47:44,128 --> 00:47:45,497
- [Crow] Hey, I'm in there.

1222
00:47:45,497 --> 00:47:46,998
Oh no, that's me here.

1223
00:47:46,998 --> 00:47:49,602
- [Tom] Let's see,
jockstrap, another jockstrap.

1224
00:47:49,602 --> 00:47:50,502
- Nothin' yet.
This guy really

1225
00:47:50,502 --> 00:47:51,337
liked jockstraps.

1226
00:47:53,038 --> 00:47:54,840
- Wait a minute.

1227
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:56,408
- [Crow] It's my brain.

1228
00:47:56,408 --> 00:47:57,242
Found it.

1229
00:47:58,877 --> 00:48:00,945
- [Chillis] Well, the
joke's on me, isn't it?

1230
00:48:00,945 --> 00:48:02,847
- You think nobody
has a brain, but you.

1231
00:48:02,847 --> 00:48:04,515
- Quite to the contrary, Bruce.

1232
00:48:04,515 --> 00:48:07,452
I'm the first to bow
to superior intellect.

1233
00:48:07,452 --> 00:48:10,055
It's just that I very rarely
encounter it. (laughs)

1234
00:48:10,055 --> 00:48:12,057
- [Tom] Well, you Schneidered
me on that one boss.

1235
00:48:12,057 --> 00:48:13,258
You shaved ol' Bruce.

1236
00:48:13,258 --> 00:48:15,293
[Bruce] Hold it, I
wanna get that shower.

1237
00:48:16,262 --> 00:48:17,495
- [Chillis] Make it fast.

1238
00:48:17,495 --> 00:48:19,330
I can't stand the odor
in here much longer.

1239
00:48:24,502 --> 00:48:25,937
Want the lights?
- Yeah.

1240
00:48:25,937 --> 00:48:28,273
- [Tom] Would you
scratch my ear.

1241
00:48:28,273 --> 00:48:30,775
- [Bruce] Nevermind, I got it.
- [Chillis] I guess with you,

1242
00:48:30,775 --> 00:48:32,210
it doesn't make any difference.

1243
00:48:32,210 --> 00:48:35,013
You can probably see
just as well in the dark.

1244
00:48:35,013 --> 00:48:36,548
- [Crow] Yep, got
me again, boss.

1245
00:48:36,548 --> 00:48:37,415
Yep, you did.

1246
00:48:39,217 --> 00:48:42,120
- [Joel] Hey, let's shower in
our clothes just for a Lark.

1247
00:48:44,455 --> 00:48:46,692
[Crow] Geez, it smells
like a locker room.

1248
00:48:46,692 --> 00:48:47,525
Oh, it is.

1249
00:48:48,460 --> 00:48:51,228
(dramatic music)

1250
00:48:56,233 --> 00:48:58,137
- [Tom] A teddy, a
jock, a side of beef,

1251
00:48:58,137 --> 00:49:00,205
Annette Funicello poster?

1252
00:49:00,205 --> 00:49:01,740
Edgar Allen Poe poetry.

1253
00:49:02,907 --> 00:49:05,643
- [Crow] Oh no, he
died of jock itch.

1254
00:49:05,643 --> 00:49:07,278
- Whatever it was, we missed it.

1255
00:49:14,385 --> 00:49:16,053
- [Tom] Return to Papyon.

1256
00:49:19,758 --> 00:49:21,360
- [Crow] A surgeon
general warning.

1257
00:49:21,360 --> 00:49:23,362
- [Tom] Hey that's
from Catalina Caper.

1258
00:49:26,998 --> 00:49:28,467
- [Joel] This is great.

1259
00:49:28,467 --> 00:49:30,135
We're having an adventure,
just like the Goonies.

1260
00:49:31,837 --> 00:49:34,338
- I wish we knew what they
took out of that locker.

1261
00:49:34,338 --> 00:49:36,708
- Maybe if we knew that,
we'd know why Sonny's dead.

1262
00:49:36,708 --> 00:49:38,543
- You think they're the ones?

1263
00:49:38,543 --> 00:49:39,978
- I don't know.

1264
00:49:39,978 --> 00:49:41,447
I don't know.

1265
00:49:41,447 --> 00:49:44,315
But ever since he joined this
gym, he seemed to change.

1266
00:49:44,315 --> 00:49:46,418
- Yeah, he got bulkier.
- Changed how?

1267
00:49:46,418 --> 00:49:47,852
- Well, he had
something on his mind.

1268
00:49:47,852 --> 00:49:49,220
- Water.
- Somethin' that was

1269
00:49:49,220 --> 00:49:51,088
really buggin' him.

1270
00:49:51,088 --> 00:49:53,825
Whenever I'd ask him
about it, he'd clam up.

1271
00:49:53,825 --> 00:49:55,260
- Maybe it was
because of his mother.

1272
00:49:55,260 --> 00:49:57,028
- [Tom] Hey, his
mother was a Saint.

1273
00:49:57,028 --> 00:49:58,430
- That's what I figured too.

1274
00:49:59,597 --> 00:50:01,265
But now.

1275
00:50:01,265 --> 00:50:02,667
- [Tom] Yeah?

1276
00:50:02,667 --> 00:50:03,502
- [Phil] I wonder.

1277
00:50:03,502 --> 00:50:04,937
- What, what?

1278
00:50:04,937 --> 00:50:06,572
- [Crow] Hey, put on
Dude Looks Like a Lady.

1279
00:50:06,572 --> 00:50:07,438
I love that.

1280
00:50:11,510 --> 00:50:14,145
All right, I'll have the pork
rind ball to lie down with

1281
00:50:14,145 --> 00:50:16,582
and a diet Coke, please.

1282
00:50:16,582 --> 00:50:18,150
- Did you ask him?

1283
00:50:18,150 --> 00:50:19,617
- Ask who what?

1284
00:50:19,617 --> 00:50:22,120
- Ask Barney about
a job, what else?

1285
00:50:22,120 --> 00:50:23,455
- No.

1286
00:50:23,455 --> 00:50:24,823
- Well, let's try now.

1287
00:50:24,823 --> 00:50:26,858
Hey, Barney.
- Google.

1288
00:50:26,858 --> 00:50:29,493
- Barney, how'd you like
to double your business?

1289
00:50:29,493 --> 00:50:31,497
- No thanks.
- What's the joke?

1290
00:50:31,497 --> 00:50:32,797
- No joke.

1291
00:50:32,797 --> 00:50:34,632
All you have to do
is hire Phil here,

1292
00:50:34,632 --> 00:50:37,068
and I'll personally guarantee
that within a month's time,

1293
00:50:37,068 --> 00:50:39,203
your business'll be doubled.

1294
00:50:39,203 --> 00:50:40,172
- Hire him as what?

1295
00:50:40,172 --> 00:50:42,240
- Well, as a singer, what else?

1296
00:50:42,240 --> 00:50:44,575
- He's lucky I let
him in here to sing.

1297
00:50:44,575 --> 00:50:46,678
- Don't worry, laughin'
boy, it won't happen again.

1298
00:50:46,678 --> 00:50:47,712
- Take it easy, Phil.

1299
00:50:48,980 --> 00:50:50,415
- Forget it.

1300
00:50:50,415 --> 00:50:51,215
- Excuse me.

1301
00:50:52,150 --> 00:50:53,118
I'm Sydney Chillis.

1302
00:50:53,118 --> 00:50:54,718
I'd like to talk with you.

1303
00:50:54,718 --> 00:50:56,320
May I buy you a drink?

1304
00:50:56,320 --> 00:50:57,622
- I'm in a hurry, Mac.

1305
00:50:57,622 --> 00:51:00,125
- It might be worth your while.

1306
00:51:00,125 --> 00:51:02,093
- [Crow] A clue, a clue, a clue.

1307
00:51:04,863 --> 00:51:08,032
That's a clue.
- Yeah.

1308
00:51:08,032 --> 00:51:10,935
- [Crow] Wow, I'm my own
Saturday night thing.

1309
00:51:10,935 --> 00:51:12,803
- [Tom] It's a
drive-up stud service.

1310
00:51:15,073 --> 00:51:16,073
- You Phil Sandifer?

1311
00:51:16,942 --> 00:51:18,777
- [Crow] You Lou Reed?

1312
00:51:18,777 --> 00:51:19,812
- Yeah, that's right.

1313
00:51:20,978 --> 00:51:24,015
- Marsha Hay, Mr.
Chillis' manicurist.

1314
00:51:30,422 --> 00:51:31,388
- [Tom] It's real.

1315
00:51:31,388 --> 00:51:32,623
I've seen these, they're nice.

1316
00:51:32,623 --> 00:51:33,925
You're a lucky woman.

1317
00:51:33,925 --> 00:51:36,093
- I guess he must
pay pretty well.

1318
00:51:36,093 --> 00:51:37,695
- It's not mine.

1319
00:51:37,695 --> 00:51:39,463
Belongs to Mr. Chillis.

1320
00:51:39,463 --> 00:51:40,965
He lets me use it for errands.

1321
00:51:42,367 --> 00:51:43,768
Get in.

1322
00:51:43,768 --> 00:51:45,370
- [Joel] Wanted, manicurist
for an evil slob.

1323
00:51:45,370 --> 00:51:46,838
- All righty.
- Photo a must.

1324
00:51:50,675 --> 00:51:52,210
- [Tom] Ooh, these
seats are hot.

1325
00:51:52,210 --> 00:51:54,045
- So you're the new singer.

1326
00:51:54,045 --> 00:51:55,980
- [Crow] Yep, Isaac
Basher, the singer.

1327
00:51:55,980 --> 00:51:57,248
- I didn't say I'd take it yet.

1328
00:51:58,950 --> 00:52:00,252
- I hope you do.

1329
00:52:00,252 --> 00:52:03,053
- [Joel] Because I want
you to go on and on.

1330
00:52:04,388 --> 00:52:06,023
- [Crow] They make
love on the highways.

1331
00:52:06,023 --> 00:52:06,958
Love on the byways.

1332
00:52:06,958 --> 00:52:09,928
Love in the streets. (laughs)

1333
00:52:11,062 --> 00:52:14,098
(swanky music)

1334
00:52:14,098 --> 00:52:16,200
- [Crow] Boy, they went all
out for this grand opening.

1335
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:18,437
- [Joel] See, you put one
foot in front of the other

1336
00:52:18,437 --> 00:52:20,972
and then you're
walking in the door.

1337
00:52:20,972 --> 00:52:22,407
- I call 'em stairs.
- Yeah.

1338
00:52:23,608 --> 00:52:24,977
- [Tom] Now I know
this is bad luck,

1339
00:52:24,977 --> 00:52:26,578
but you're already in the movie.

1340
00:52:30,182 --> 00:52:31,983
- This'll all be finished
by tomorrow night.

1341
00:52:33,150 --> 00:52:34,118
Wait here a second.

1342
00:52:37,488 --> 00:52:39,590
- Beetle Bailey,
what's he up to now?

1343
00:52:39,590 --> 00:52:40,592
- Bring the singer?

1344
00:52:40,592 --> 00:52:41,660
- Yeah, where's Sydney.

1345
00:52:41,660 --> 00:52:43,428
- Where do you think?

1346
00:52:43,428 --> 00:52:44,462
- All right to go in?

1347
00:52:44,462 --> 00:52:45,430
- You modest?

1348
00:52:45,430 --> 00:52:46,732
- [Crow] What do you think?

1349
00:52:49,300 --> 00:52:50,702
- Sydney, singer's here.

1350
00:52:52,170 --> 00:52:53,772
- [Crow] What, are they
in a double-wide trailer?

1351
00:52:56,040 --> 00:52:57,275
- [Tom] Hi, still here.

1352
00:53:00,845 --> 00:53:01,980
- Get him outta here.

1353
00:53:01,980 --> 00:53:03,648
- Toga, toga.
- Get him outta here.

1354
00:53:03,648 --> 00:53:05,883
- Toga, toga.
- Calm down.

1355
00:53:05,883 --> 00:53:07,552
He's having one of his fits.
What on earth is wrong?

1356
00:53:07,552 --> 00:53:09,053
- That kid out there,
he's the one who come in

1357
00:53:09,053 --> 00:53:10,522
about DeMarco's locker.

1358
00:53:10,522 --> 00:53:11,990
- So?
- But he had the key.

1359
00:53:11,990 --> 00:53:13,225
Maybe he knew-

1360
00:53:13,225 --> 00:53:14,558
- Come over here and
start on my back.

1361
00:53:14,558 --> 00:53:16,628
- [Tom] And get me my
Filipino house boy.

1362
00:53:23,535 --> 00:53:26,137
- Now, Bruce, you don't
think for a minute

1363
00:53:26,137 --> 00:53:28,340
I'd blunder
haphazardly into this.

1364
00:53:29,607 --> 00:53:32,110
I've done some
checking on this boy.

1365
00:53:32,110 --> 00:53:35,347
He was a friend of Leonard's,
a very close friend.

1366
00:53:35,347 --> 00:53:37,948
So you see, it's only natural
he'd want to clean out

1367
00:53:37,948 --> 00:53:39,150
the boy's locker.

1368
00:53:39,150 --> 00:53:40,952
- Yeah, but suppose
he sees me here.

1369
00:53:40,952 --> 00:53:42,187
- He's going to see you.

1370
00:53:43,488 --> 00:53:45,490
- But he'll get wise to every-
- Keep working.

1371
00:53:45,490 --> 00:53:47,858
You've over-stimulated
your heart.

1372
00:53:47,858 --> 00:53:48,893
- And grossed us all out.
- I don't want you

1373
00:53:48,893 --> 00:53:49,727
standing around.

1374
00:53:51,028 --> 00:53:53,298
You're my personal masseur.

1375
00:53:53,298 --> 00:53:55,933
Who's a more logical
candidate for that position,

1376
00:53:55,933 --> 00:53:57,735
but a gym manager.

1377
00:53:57,735 --> 00:54:01,272
And suppose, just
suppose he is suspicious.

1378
00:54:01,272 --> 00:54:03,342
What a better place to
have him than right here

1379
00:54:03,342 --> 00:54:04,542
under our noses.

1380
00:54:05,943 --> 00:54:09,913
Easy, Bruce, your little
tantrum was all for nothing.

1381
00:54:09,913 --> 00:54:11,415
- [Tom] He's basting in butter.

1382
00:54:13,083 --> 00:54:14,685
- [Bruce] It's okay,
he's your responsibility.

1383
00:54:14,685 --> 00:54:16,622
- Of course he's
my responsibility.

1384
00:54:17,788 --> 00:54:18,723
- [Joel] I promise to
feed him twice a day

1385
00:54:18,723 --> 00:54:19,992
and take him for walks.

1386
00:54:19,992 --> 00:54:20,792
- Unless we have someone
to make the deliveries,

1387
00:54:20,792 --> 00:54:22,327
we're out of business.

1388
00:54:22,327 --> 00:54:24,562
Unfortunately I don't have
the stomach for that sort of

1389
00:54:24,562 --> 00:54:27,098
thing, and you
don't have the eyes.

1390
00:54:27,098 --> 00:54:28,633
- [Crow] You got me.

1391
00:54:28,633 --> 00:54:30,902
- Bruce, let's be honest.

1392
00:54:30,902 --> 00:54:32,170
- This movie sucks.
- Neither of us

1393
00:54:32,170 --> 00:54:33,772
can carry a tune. (laughs)

1394
00:54:33,772 --> 00:54:35,073
- [Tom] Oh yeah, that too.

1395
00:54:36,708 --> 00:54:37,542
- Okay, handsome.

1396
00:54:38,577 --> 00:54:39,777
- Okay.

1397
00:54:39,777 --> 00:54:41,412
- You smell like
Captain Kangaroo.

1398
00:54:43,382 --> 00:54:46,283
- [Joel] Come in, Jedidiah,
pour yourself some Paul Masson.

1399
00:54:46,283 --> 00:54:47,918
- Sorry to keep you
waiting, Philip.

1400
00:54:47,918 --> 00:54:50,322
I was in the middle
of a steam bath.

1401
00:54:50,322 --> 00:54:51,555
- That's all right.

1402
00:54:51,555 --> 00:54:53,792
- No it's not, it's
downright rude.

1403
00:54:53,792 --> 00:54:55,093
I hope you will forgive me.

1404
00:54:56,928 --> 00:54:58,397
Now let's see.

1405
00:54:58,397 --> 00:54:59,930
You know Marsha.

1406
00:54:59,930 --> 00:55:02,067
The gentlemen on the chair
is Mr. Green, my masseur.

1407
00:55:02,067 --> 00:55:02,900
- We've met.

1408
00:55:04,335 --> 00:55:05,203
- Oh, you have?

1409
00:55:10,008 --> 00:55:12,377
- You're the one who came in
about the DeMarco kid's locker.

1410
00:55:12,377 --> 00:55:13,678
- [Tom] Yeah, and you're
the one who can't see beyond

1411
00:55:13,678 --> 00:55:15,313
his nose.
- That's right, I'm the one.

1412
00:55:15,313 --> 00:55:16,815
- Friend of his was
enrolled in the gym.

1413
00:55:16,815 --> 00:55:18,717
Doin' real fine too.

1414
00:55:18,717 --> 00:55:20,018
Had an auto accident.

1415
00:55:20,018 --> 00:55:22,820
- I certainly hope it
wasn't anything serious.

1416
00:55:22,820 --> 00:55:23,955
- He died.

1417
00:55:23,955 --> 00:55:25,457
- My condolences.

1418
00:55:25,457 --> 00:55:27,292
What can you say in a
situation like this?

1419
00:55:27,292 --> 00:55:29,093
Words are so meaningless.

1420
00:55:29,093 --> 00:55:30,328
- [Crow] I'd like to
say a really bad joke.

1421
00:55:30,328 --> 00:55:32,263
- Well, what do you
think of my club?

1422
00:55:32,263 --> 00:55:33,865
- [Crow] Foot.

1423
00:55:33,865 --> 00:55:35,933
- I think it's very nice.

1424
00:55:35,933 --> 00:55:38,437
- I put in a great
deal of thought into
making the High Note

1425
00:55:38,437 --> 00:55:40,538
an inducement for our
young people to gather

1426
00:55:40,538 --> 00:55:42,873
for wholesome fun and music.

1427
00:55:42,873 --> 00:55:45,077
- And evil.
- Now look, Mr. Chillis.

1428
00:55:45,077 --> 00:55:46,310
You know my problem.

1429
00:55:46,310 --> 00:55:48,813
I'm on probation,
no driver's license.

1430
00:55:48,813 --> 00:55:51,682
I explained that last night.

1431
00:55:51,682 --> 00:55:53,518
- Indeed, you did.

1432
00:55:53,518 --> 00:55:56,653
Just, as I promised, I've
come up with a solution.

1433
00:55:56,653 --> 00:55:59,357
- [Joel] And we'll inject
it straight into your head.

1434
00:55:59,357 --> 00:56:01,358
- I've got something
interesting to show you.

1435
00:56:01,358 --> 00:56:03,027
- [Tom] Something festive.

1436
00:56:03,027 --> 00:56:03,962
- [Chillis] Come along.

1437
00:56:05,397 --> 00:56:06,663
- [Tom] Yeah, we're meeting
Peter Lawford for dinner.

1438
00:56:06,663 --> 00:56:08,933
- The bartender at
the Rainbow Gardens,

1439
00:56:08,933 --> 00:56:12,637
he told me you've earned all
kinds of honors racing cars.

1440
00:56:12,637 --> 00:56:14,338
- Well yeah, I won a few drags.

1441
00:56:14,338 --> 00:56:16,007
- That's why I think you'll
appreciate what I have

1442
00:56:16,007 --> 00:56:16,842
to show you.

1443
00:56:18,843 --> 00:56:20,645
Well, what do you think of it?

1444
00:56:20,645 --> 00:56:22,913
- [Joel] It's a tiny
statue of Saint Francis.

1445
00:56:22,913 --> 00:56:23,815
- You're kiddin'?

1446
00:56:24,982 --> 00:56:26,985
- Wait, my boy, never
jump at conclusions.

1447
00:56:26,985 --> 00:56:28,352
Open the hood.

1448
00:56:28,352 --> 00:56:29,153
Go ahead.

1449
00:56:31,722 --> 00:56:36,627
- Oh my God!
- Oh that's terrible!

1450
00:56:36,627 --> 00:56:38,062
- An espresso machine?
- That's fantastic!

1451
00:56:38,062 --> 00:56:40,698
- Well, a house like this
needs expert driving.

1452
00:56:41,800 --> 00:56:43,367
- Wanna bet I could handle her?

1453
00:56:44,335 --> 00:56:45,803
- I'm sure you could.

1454
00:56:45,803 --> 00:56:47,572
- [Tom] Have you ever
thought about being evil?

1455
00:56:47,572 --> 00:56:48,740
I mean really evil?

1456
00:56:50,108 --> 00:56:51,342
- Oh, what's the
use Mr. Chillis?

1457
00:56:51,342 --> 00:56:53,645
Why are we even talkin'
about a job out here?

1458
00:56:54,978 --> 00:56:56,613
- Come along to my office.

1459
00:56:56,613 --> 00:56:57,415
